<title>NETHERLANDS: HEIJMANS PLUNGES ON DISAPPOINTING H1 NET.</title>
<headline>HEIJMANS PLUNGES ON DISAPPOINTING H1 NET.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch construction firm Heijmans NV plunged 7.5 percent on Thursday after the group announced first half profits at the lower end of analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>By 1115 GMT the stock was down 11.00 guilders at 148.00, off an earlier low of 145.00.</p>
<p>The group announced first half profits of 12.5 million guilders, and reiterated its previous forecast of a clear growth of profits and sales for the whole of 1996.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected profits of 11 to 15.4 million, with the consensus at 13.9 million.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
